# South Australian civil registration — the whole Zubrinich limb, three generations.
#
# 16 September 2026, work list row 57 item 3. THIRTY-FIVE births, ELEVEN
# marriages, FOURTEEN deaths. Read from the index rows themselves, which in this
# collection carry BOTH PARENTS on a birth and the SPOUSE on a marriage — so no
# transcript is needed for the core of it.
#
# THIS IS THE RECORD THE ELECTORAL ROLLS COULD NOT BE. The rolls give an address
# and a trade and leave you to guess who is whose. These name the parents.
# Together they close the Australian limb: John and Rose marry in 1884, twelve
# children follow to 1909, and their sons' households are the addresses in the
# 1939-43 rolls.
#
# AND THEY CORRECT TWO READINGS MADE FROM THE ROLLS THE SAME DAY. Thomas Leo and
# Una Blanche were NOT newly married between the 1939 and 1941 rolls — they
# married in 1912 and had nine children; the household simply MOVED from 11 Queen
# Street to 30 Beach Road. Leonard Francis and Asta Louise married in 1936 at
# ADELAIDE, not between the 1939 and 1943 rolls. Both errors came from reading
# the roll's «household members» field as a household. It is not one.
#
